          "kicker": "Refereeing revamp",
          "heading": "Steve Borthwick secures rule alignment boost for England World Cup campaign",
          "body": "Steve Borthwick has secured a boost to his preparations for next year's tournament after Prem Rugby agreed to overhaul refereeing interpretations for the coming season. The Guardian understands agreement has been reached to better align domestic officiating with the international game, specifically targeting the offside line, the scrum's brake-foot law, and the breakdown. Borthwick previously met with directors of rugby following concerns over the consistency of officiating, aiming to mount a serious challenge to South Africa's supremacy in Australia."
