      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "WXV opening",
          "heading": "Ireland Women head coach Scott Bemand rues frustrating defeat against USA",
          "body": "Ireland Women head coach Scott Bemand admitted their 40-36 defeat against the USA in the WXV Global Series opener at Tallaght Stadium was \"a game we should have won\". Bemand's side surrendered a 19-point advantage after leading 31-12 in the second half, as a loss of discipline and four unanswered tries from the visitors turned the fixture. A late try from Dorothy Wall in the red gave Ireland a final chance to snatch victory, but the USA defence held firm."
        },
